{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 30, :comments ["<b>And how will Pharaoh listen to me.</b> This passage is itself the one above: 'the Israelites did not listen to me' — only, above he was brief in his words until he explained to you 'these are the heads of their ancestral houses,' to know who Moses and Aaron, the speakers, are; and afterwards he goes back and repeats them in order to write the command and the matters in sequence, and to connect 'and Aaron your brother shall be your prophet' to 'for I am of uncircumcised lips.'"], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:56:24.331508234Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}